NAME
    extract - extract or materialize one physical artifact format

SYNOPSIS
    extract <format> <artifact> <destination>

DESCRIPTION
    extract performs raw physical artifact extraction or materialization. It does
    not interpret package catalog metadata, select package components, choose a
    package useful root or apply package overlays.

    <format> identifies the physical artifact format, <artifact> is the input
    file and <destination> is an existing real directory receiving the raw
    result.

    Supported archive/container formats are:
        tar
        tar.gz  tgz
        tar.bz2 tar.bzip2 tbz tbz2
        tar.xz  txz
        tar.zst tzst
        zip jar war
        7z 7zip
        dmg
        deb
        pkg

    Supported single-stream compression formats are:
        gzip gz
        bzip bzip2 bz2
        xz
        zstd zst

    appimage and executable are opaque physical materialization formats.
    appimage copies the artifact unchanged into the destination. executable does
    the same and ensures the copied output is executable.

    dmg extracts the DMG contents only. It does not interpret .app, .pkg or any
    other object found inside the image.

    pkg expands one Apple flat installer package into its raw expanded package
    structure. It does not select a component or Payload and never runs installer
    scripts.

    A single-stream format creates one decompressed file in the destination,
    deriving its name from the artifact basename and compression suffix. The
    output pathname must not already exist.

    For zip, jar and war archives, unsafe member names are rejected before
    extraction: absolute paths, parent-directory traversal and backslash
    pathnames are not accepted. Existing symbolic links in the target path of
    any ZIP-family member are rejected before extraction to avoid redirecting
    output outside the requested destination.

    TAR and compressed TAR archives also receive member-path preflight checks
    before their tar backend is invoked, including rejection of absolute or
    parent-traversing members and existing symbolic links in target paths.
    These checks do not cover archive-created links, concurrent filesystem
    changes or other extraction backends.

    Backend utilities are selected according to the requested format and host
    capabilities. Missing required backends cause failure.

OPERANDS
    <format>
        Explicit physical artifact format.
    <artifact>
        Existing readable regular file.
    <destination>
        Existing real directory receiving raw materialized content.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m extract [arguments].


EXIT STATUS
    0   Success.
    2   Invalid invocation or unsupported format.
    3   ZIP member enumeration failed.
    4   ZIP member pathname rejected as unsafe.
    5   ZIP member target uses an existing symbolic link.
    6   ZIP member preflight failed unexpectedly.
    7   TAR member enumeration failed.
    8   TAR member pathname rejected as unsafe.
    9   TAR member target uses an existing symbolic link.
    10  TAR member preflight failed unexpectedly.
    Other non-zero status indicates artifact, destination, backend or extraction
        failure.
